WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.084 --> 00:00:03.570
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.980
- Just like its name says,

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.860
NATO is a North Atlantic organization.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.850
Here's the Atlantic,

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.030
and all of these blue flags
represent NATO countries.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.430
The whole reason that the
organization came together

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.190
in the first place was to
protect against possible threats

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.540
from the Soviet Union,

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.820
and it's now protecting against Russia.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.190
But lately, NATO has been
ramping up partnerships

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.740
on the other side of the
world in the Pacific,

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.710
and challenges from China
are the big reason why.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.900
So how do NATO partnerships work

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.390
and what do they mean for both NATO allies

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.983
and potential adversaries?

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.170
Just weeks before Russia
launched its full scale invasion

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:43.020
of Ukraine, Presidents Xi
Jinping and Vladimir Putin

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.190
held a summit.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.140
They released this joint statement

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.090
which made headlines around the world.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.350
They declared that the friendship

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.883
between the two states has
no limits, and they said,

00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:55.140
that the sides oppose
further enlargement of NATO

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.060
and call on the North Atlantic alliance

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:01.350
to abandon its ideologized,
Cold War approaches.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.625
Russia and China see NATO
expansion as a huge threat.

00:01:04.625 --> 00:01:08.292
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:11.031 --> 00:01:14.698
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.110
But ever since Russia launched
its full scale invasion

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.023
of Ukraine, just weeks after
that statement was put out,

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.970
NATO has gotten both bigger and stronger.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.550
Not only did Russia's
neighbors, Finland and Sweden,

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.020
move to join the alliance,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.330
but some of the countries
in China's backyard

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.390
moved to strengthen their
relationships with NATO too.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.860
I'm talking about the Pacific,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.340
South Korea, Japan New
Zealand, and Australia.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.080
While they aren't seeking full membership

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.090
they worry that what's
happening in Ukraine,

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.760
could also happen here in Taiwan,

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.180
the self-ruled island that
Beijing claims as part of China

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.220
and has threatened to take by force.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.150
Taiwan is tiny,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.980
but it produces a majority of the world's

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.750
advanced semiconductors.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.270
Those are the microchips
that power our electronics,

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.600
our cars, our medical devices,
basically our whole lives.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.180
And a war over Taiwan
could devastate economies,

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.400
no matter where they're
located in the world.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.420
And that's why we keep hearing

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.970
the NATO Secretary General say this.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:16.241
- Security is not regional,
security is global.

00:02:16.241 --> 00:02:20.490
What happens in the Pacific
matters for Europe, for NATO,

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.790
and what happens in Europe
matters for the Indo-Pacific.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.950
- For the past two years,
leaders of the so-called

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.950
Asia Pacific four have
attended major NATO summits

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:29.910
and events,

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:32.339
and those countries' militaries
have conducted exercises

00:02:32.339 --> 00:02:33.930
alongside NATO.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.940
These developments have
frustrated Beijing,

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.720
which says NATO is intervening
in regional affairs

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.510
and inciting bloc confrontation.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.810
Now, NATO maintains that
it is a defensive alliance

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.310
and according to its chief.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:52.310
- We will be remiss if we
did not expose the challenges

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:57.390
that China poses to our
security, to our values,

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.220
and to our interests.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.010
- Experts say those challenges
aren't just in Taiwan,

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.930
they're happening all over the world,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.960
like in Europe where Chinese
firms own stakes in ports,

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.460
roads and railways.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.500
In Africa, where the Chinese have stakes

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.370
in critical mining operations
and technology infrastructure.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.203
In the Arctic,

00:03:15.203 --> 00:03:17.040
where China is developing gas projects

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.690
and transportation corridors.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.970
And in space and cyberspace,

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.540
where Beijing has been advancing
its military capabilities.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.070
Last year for the first time,

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.230
NATO's concerns about China appeared

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:31.380
in its main guiding document,
The Strategic Concept.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.982
NATO says China is trying
to control key technology

00:03:33.982 --> 00:03:35.580
and industrial sectors,

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.060
is using economic leverage to
create strategic dependencies

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.140
and is trying to subvert

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.420
the rules-based international order.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.030
China says NATO's concerns disregard facts

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.590
and confuse right and wrong.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:47.850
But here's the thing,

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.070
not every NATO member is on the same page

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:52.470
when it comes to how far
the alliance should go

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:53.760
to counter China.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.610
If a NATO member like the
US gets involved in a war

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:59.910
in the Pacific, allies aren't
obligated to participate,

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.520
since Article 5 only
considers an armed attack

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.700
against one or more allies
in Europe or North America

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.170
as an attack against them all.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.630
Plus different NATO
countries have varying levels

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.580
of interconnectedness with China.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.760
So some are more hesitant than
others to ramp up pressure.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:18.030
For example, NATO has discussed
setting up a liaison office

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.714
in Tokyo, but so far those
plans have been blocked

00:04:20.714 --> 00:04:23.880
by French officials and
President Emmanuel Macron says

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.580
that enlarging NATO's
spectrum and geography

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.870
would be a mistake.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.730
With or without physical offices,

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.370
experts say that NATO and
its partners could benefit

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.890
from collaborating on
things like cybersecurity,

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:38.940
space security, disinformation,
and even climate change.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.340
But when it comes to a
potential war over Taiwan,

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.470
would NATO members and partners send aid

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:44.940
like they have to Ukraine

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.280
or perhaps get more involved in the fight?

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.980
Their possible role
remains a major question

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.570
and is something that the United States

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:52.980
is still trying to work out.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.610
- The defense of freedom is not
the work of a day or a year,

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:00.123
it's the calling of our
lifetime, of all time.

